---
layout: changelog
title: "Connect Resend in one click for custom SMTP and Messaging"
date: 2026-09-22
cover: /images/blog/announcing-resend-one-click-setup/cover.avif
tags: auth, messaging, console, integrations
---

The Appwrite Cloud Console can now set up Resend for you. Click **Connect with Resend**, authorize Appwrite, and pick a verified domain. Appwrite creates a sending-only API key restricted to that domain, named `Appwrite SMTP: <project name>`, and writes the rest of the configuration itself.

On the project **Settings** > **SMTP** tab, the new **One-click setup** card fills in the [custom SMTP settings](/docs/products/auth/message-templates#smtp-one-click-setup) with `smtp.resend.com`, port `587`, the `resend` username, TLS, and the new key as the password, then enables the custom server. In **Messaging** > **Providers**, the same card on the [Resend provider](/docs/products/messaging/resend#one-click-setup) generates the API key and fills the sender fields before you click **Create provider**. One authorization covers both, and Appwrite revokes any key it generated that never gets saved.

